# Client-app installers are BINARIES built from droplet-windows /
# droplet-android — they are never committed here (they'd bloat every
# clone, and this is not the repo that builds them).
#
# Two things put an installer here: an operator running
# scripts/app-downloads/stage.sh on the box, and (WARP-3120) the box's own
# OTA update, for the installers clients.lock.json pins. No image-build step
# or setup.sh path does. If you are reading this because /downloads is
# empty, see README.md; `bash scripts/app-downloads/audit.sh` will tell you
# what this release is supposed to carry.
#
# Tracked here: only the hand-authored side of the contract, the docs,
# EXPECTED — the per-platform declaration the auditor reconciles against
# what is actually staged — and clients.lock.json, the pinned installers.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
!platforms.example.json
!EXPECTED
!clients.lock.json
